body:
**Feature request**

I'd like to give the main index a label when using a custom autocomplete widget with multiple indices. Additional indices added in the widget can have a label and I would like to be able to label the main index for output on the front end also.

Here's my code:

```
import instantsearch from 'instantsearch.js';
import { connectAutocomplete } from 'instantsearch.js/es/connectors';

import searchClient from '../../algolia/searchClient';
import { autocomplete } from '../../algolia/widgets';

const search = instantsearch({
  indexName: 'destination',
  searchClient,
});

const customAutocomplete = connectAutocomplete(autocomplete);

search.addWidget(
  customAutocomplete({
    container: document.querySelector('#my-search-box'),
    indices: [
      { label: 'Hotels', value: 'hotel' },
    ],
  }),
);

search.start();
```

I pass in the index "destination" as my main index, then add an additional index of "hotels" to my custom autocomplete widget. I am able to label this one but not the main "destination" index, and on the front end the label returns "primary".

I didn't find any way to do this in the docs/issues/stack overflow. Apologies in advance if I've missed it.
